  <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
  <itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
  <description><![CDATA[<div>
<p>So there we have it - an FPL season for the AGES...</p><p>Congratulations Arsenal - Champions for the first time in 22 years! And on the other side of North London - RELIEF! Spurs stay up, so De Zerbi lives to fight another season, despite some nervy moments at the Tottenham Hotspur Stadium earlier today. Elsewhere, Sunderland - yes SUNDERLAND - make Europe, but Chelsea miss out altogether. With Alonso coming in over the summer though, does that make them more attractive potentially for next season's FPL.</p><p>We also reveal what we all thought was going to happen back in GW1, when we made our pre-season predictions!</p><p>A massive THANK YOU for all your support watching, liking and sharing our videos!</p><p>__________________________<br> 🚀 Support FPL Family on Patreon:</p></div><ul>
<li><p>Exclusive FREE Podcasts every week looking ahead to the next GW</p></li>
<li><p>Manager of the Month Competitions  - MONTHLY PRIZES!</p></li>
<li><p>Zoom Video Chats with Lee and Sam</p></li>
<li><p>Slack Chat community with other FPL Managers</p></li>
</ul><div>
