<item>
  <title>S9 Ep36: Arsenal Champions Elect? West Ham FUMING with VAR! FPL GW36-GW37 Fantasy Premier League</title>
  <link>https://audioboom.com/posts/8901756</link>
  <itunes:episode>36</itunes:episode>
  <itunes:title>Arsenal Champions Elect? West Ham FUMING with VAR! FPL GW36-GW37 Fantasy Premier League</itunes:title>
  <itunes:season>9</itunes:season>
  <enclosure url="https://audioboom.com/posts/8901756.mp3?modified=1778450292&amp;sid=5010221&amp;source=rss" length="75980002" type="audio/mpeg" />
  <itunes:image href="https://audioboom.com/i/42921105.jpg" />
  <itunes:duration>4744</itunes:duration>
  <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
  <itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
  <description><![CDATA[<div>
<p>WOW - what an end to a dramatic weekend, and with Spurs still to play Leeds on Monday night, it's Arsenal who take a massive step towards the title and it's West Ham licking their wounds from a tough-to-take VAR call at the death. </p><p>A Double Gameweek in name only for Lee and Sam, as neither went with any Palace players for their two games in GW36. Both went all-in on City though, with mixed success. Elsewhere Liverpool and Chelsea play out a draw at Anfield, Brighton smash Wolves and Bournemouth continue their push for European football with a decent 0-1 away win at Fulham. We talk through our scores, rank updates and differentials for that final push in GWs 37-38.</p><p>A massive THANK YOU for all your support watching, liking and sharing our videos!</p><p>__________________________<br> 🚀 Support FPL Family on Patreon:</p></div><ul>
<li><p>Exclusive FREE Podcasts every week looking ahead to the next GW</p></li>
<li><p>Manager of the Month Competitions  - MONTHLY PRIZES!</p></li>
<li><p>Zoom Video Chats with Lee and Sam</p></li>
<li><p>Slack Chat community with other FPL Managers</p></li>
</ul><div>
